  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Diaspora investment mechanism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &quot;Strengthening UK-Albania Diaspora Engagement for Sustainable Development&quot; aims to connect Albanians living in the United Kingdom with communities in Northern Albania to support sustainable local development. It establishes a digital platform that allows diaspora members to invest, share knowledge, and collaborate on social and economic projects. By creating legal, transparent pathways for engagement, the project strengthens local economies, supports entrepreneurship, and encourages positive contributions to communities of origin. Northern Albania has experienced significant migration, leaving some communities reliant on remittances and vulnerable to economic fragility. Implemented by the International Organization for Migration Tirana in partnership with the British Chamber of Commerce in Albania, interventions seek to strengthen engagement between the United Kingdom-based Albanian diaspora and local communities in Northern Albania. The platform facilitates financial investment, knowledge transfer, mentorship, and community support, providing visible and legal alternatives to irregular migration. The project also builds the capacity of local communities, small businesses, and municipalities to effectively use the platform, ensuring sustainable development benefits are maximized. Through this initiative, diaspora members can participate in investments, support local entrepreneurs, and share expertise, while local communities gain access to financial resources, training, and guidance for project implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
